* STM32 DAC to Eurorack Output Stage MFB Simulation
* 
* Circuit Characteristics:
* - Op-amp supply: +/-12V
* - Input: 0V to 3.3V DAC signal, centered on 1.65V for AC/transient tests
* - Standard E12 series resistors and E6 series capacitors
* - 2nd-order multiple-feedback low-pass filter, fc ~19.4kHz, Q~0.706
* - Output range near +/-10V, with a 100 ohm / 1nF output isolation pole

VIN IN 0 DC 1.65 AC 1 SIN(1.65 1.65 1k)
VPLUS VP 0 DC 12
VMINUS VN 0 DC -12
VADC 3V3 0 DC 3.3

.include "antialiasing_input_stage.lib"

* 1.405V non-inverting reference centers the amplified DAC range around 0V
R_REF_PU 3V3 VREF_TOP 47k
R_REF_SER VREF_TOP VREF 5.6k
R_REF_PD VREF 0 39k
C_REF VREF 0 10u

* 2nd-order inverting MFB low-pass, with R4 split into E12 series values
R1 IN N_MFB 100k
R3 N_MFB N_INV 22k
R4A OUT N_FB 560k
R4B N_FB N_MFB 56k
C2 N_MFB 0 330p
C5 OUT N_INV 15p

* Bipolar-supply amplifier; output polarity is inverted relative to the DAC input
XU1 VREF N_INV VP VN OUT RRIO_OPAMP

* Output isolation and capacitive-load pole
R_OUT OUT DAC_OUT 100
C_OUT DAC_OUT 0 1n

.control
* AC frequency sweep from 10 Hz to 1 MHz (100 points per decade)
ac dec 100 10 1Meg
set wr_singlescale
wrdata ac_sim.txt v(DAC_OUT) v(OUT) v(IN)

* Transient simulation over 5 ms (5 cycles of 1 kHz 0-3.3V DAC input)
tran 1u 5m 0 1u
set wr_singlescale
wrdata tran_sim.txt v(IN) v(OUT) v(DAC_OUT) v(N_INV) v(N_MFB)
quit
.endc

.end
